Apple plans to allow third-party AI chatbots to integrate with <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> in <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, reports <em><a href="https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-03-26/apple-plans-to-open-up-siri-to-rival-ai-assistants-beyond-chatgpt-in-ios-27">Bloomberg</a></em>. Apple already has a partnership with OpenAI that lets &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; hand questions off to ChatGPT, but Apple will expand that integration to other companies like Google and Anthropic.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/01/Gemini-Siri-Feature.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1032275" /><br/>
An iPhone user with the Claude or Gemini app installed will be able to send questions to those chatbots, like how the current ChatGPT feature works. Right now, if a user has a question that &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; cannot handle, &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; suggests sending it to ChatGPT. Users can also ask &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; to query ChatGPT.<br/>
<br/>
iPhone users will be able to select which services they want to use inside &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; through "Extensions" options coming to &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, iPadOS 27, and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/macos-27/">macOS 27</a>. The options will be available in the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-intelligence/">Apple Intelligence</a> and &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; section of the Settings app, with Apple providing download links for chatbot apps.<br/>
<br/>
AI apps installed through the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/app-store/">App Store</a> will be able to work with &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;, including with Apple's planned &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; app and other &zwnj;Apple Intelligence&zwnj; features. <em>Bloomberg</em> suggests that expanding &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; integration to other chatbots will allow Apple to generate more money from third-party AI subscriptions made through the &zwnj;App Store&zwnj;. AI companies will need to enable support for the new feature in &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
Apple is still planning for a full &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; overhaul, and it will release its own chatbot version of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; based on Google's Gemini models. Extensions will simply give users the option to direct requests to their favorite chatbot instead of &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
OpenAI will no longer have an exclusive partnership with Apple when the change is made in &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;. While most AI companies have not complained about the &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; ChatGPT integration, Elon Musk's xAI startup sued Apple and OpenAI, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2025/08/25/elon-musk-apple-lawsuit-grok-x/">accusing the two companies</a> of conspiring to "ensure their continued dominance" in the AI market. Musk has been vocal about wanting Grok to be available on the iPhone alongside ChatGPT.<br/>
<br/>
Apple has been considering allowing other companies to integrate with &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; for some time, and it was previously working on a deal that would allow &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; to hand queries to Gemini.<br/>
<br/>
Apple plans to announce the new &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; and the third-party integration option when it unveils &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; at the June 8 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/wwdc/">WWDC 2026</a> keynote.<div class="linkback">Related Roundup: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a></div><div class="linkback">Tag: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/03/26/apple-ios-27-siri-chatbot-integration/">Apple Plans to Let Rival AI Chatbots Integrate With Siri in iOS 27</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/apple-plans-to-let-rival-ai-chatbots-integrate-with-siri-in-ios-27.2479978/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>